      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Camera-driven size changes must never share a CSS transition channel with discrete semantic-level folds, and the wheel throttle must survive re-renders during an active zoom gesture",
        "body": "Bug report: \"weird zoomy shit\" — jittery/laggy rendering during rapid wheel-zoom in the workspace. Both causes below were independently verified against current code (exact lines), not assumed from a paraphrase.\n\nROOT CAUSE 1 — width/height animate on every zoom tick, fighting the immediate value:\ncomponents/GraphEditor/components/WorkspaceLayer.js:522 computes `const width = b.width * zoom, height = b.height * zoom;` fresh every render — changes continuously as zoom changes. Line 569-570 applies `transition: foldTransition(instance.instanceId)` to that same box, and foldTransition (line 218-219) is `'width 260ms ease, height 260ms ease'` for every instance except the one being hand-dragged (manipulatingInstanceId, set only by drag/resize — never by camera zoom, see the comment at lines 213-216). So every wheel tick sets a new width/height target while the browser is still easing toward the previous tick's target — the box perpetually chases a moving target. The comment block makes the original intent explicit: this transition was built for the semantic fold (glyph/icon/summary/detail), and position (left/top) was deliberately left untransitioned for exactly this reason (\"position is never animated... should just land there, not visibly travel there\") — width/height never got the same treatment.\n\nThe identical pattern exists a second time, independently: PassiveGraphSemanticView (also in WorkspaceLayer.js, lines 128-186ish) receives the same `transition` prop and computes `width: bounds.width * zoom` / `height: bounds.height * zoom` inline at lines 147-148 and again ~166-182 for the minimap/glyph branches. Same bug, same file, second render path.\n\nROOT CAUSE 2 — the wheel listener's throttle state is torn down and rebuilt on every render, not intermittently:\ncomponents/GraphEditor/hooks/useGraphWorkspace.js:1066 — the hook returns `{ ...apiRef.current, instances: ..., ... }`, a brand-new object literal EVERY render, unmemoized. components/NodeGraph/NodeGraph.js:400-402 — `handleWorkspaceWheelZoom` depends on `[viewportSize, workspace]`, so it's a new function every render too. components/NodeGraph/PanZoomLayer.js:304-404 — the wheel-handling effect (which owns closure-local `accumulatedDelta`/`isThrottling`/`throttleTimeout` state and a hand-rolled 16ms throttle + 100ms trailing debounce) depends on `[setZoom, onPanZoom, onWheelZoom, zoomAbout]` (line 404). Because `onWheelZoom` is new every render, this effect's cleanup-and-reinstall fires every render — during an active zoom gesture (which itself triggers renders via setZoom), every render throws away in-flight accumulated wheel delta and any pending throttle timeout, then reinstalls a fresh DOM listener. Not occasional — constant, for the whole duration of any zoom gesture.\n\nConfirmed but ranked lower: reflowWorkspaceInstances()/presentWorkspaceInstances() do real geometry work on every zoom tick (bridge/portal adjacency, membrane recompute). This amplifies jank from causes 1 and 2 but is not independently causal — do not optimize this first.",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Width/height transitions apply only on a discrete semantic-level change, never on a continuous zoom-driven size change",
          "The wheel-handling effect in PanZoomLayer.js no longer tears down and reinstalls on every render during an active zoom gesture",
          "Rapid wheel-zoom across semantic band thresholds (0.10/0.24/0.48/0.82) with multiple graphs open shows no visible jitter or lag",
          "Full test suite stays green (979/979 as of this task graph’s authoring)"
        ],
