      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Stop transitioning width/height on continuous zoom-driven changes",
        "body": "In WorkspaceLayer.js, the width/height transition (foldTransition, lines 218-219) needs to apply only when the semantic level actually changed since the last render — never when the same level is just tracking continuous zoom. Two candidate designs, both real, pick one:\n(a) Track each instance's previous _workspaceSemanticLevel in a ref; only include width/height in the transition string when the level differs from last render, otherwise 'none'. Narrower, more surgical.\n(b) Move the discrete fold onto an inner element's transform: scale() instead of the outer box's width/height, so continuous zoom (left/top/width/height, all immediate) and discrete folding (transform, animated) never share a CSS channel again. More architecturally clean, touches more render paths.\nThis is the open design question on this graph — decide there before implementing.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Width/height changes driven purely by continuous zoom are never animated",
          "A genuine semantic-level crossing (e.g. icon -> summary) still animates smoothly",
          "The fix is applied consistently, not just to the common case"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
