      "data": {
        "title": "Stabilize handleWorkspaceWheelZoom so the wheel effect stops churning",
        "body": "In NodeGraph.js:400-402, change handleWorkspaceWheelZoom's dependency from the whole workspace object to the one method it actually calls: workspace?.applyZoomGesture. First verify apiRef.current.applyZoomGesture in useGraphWorkspace.js is itself a referentially stable function across renders (it's assigned via useRef, so it likely is — confirm, don't assume). If it isn't stable either, that's a second, deeper fix (memoizing more of useGraphWorkspace.js's return value), out of scope for this narrow fix unless task 3 proves it necessary.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "onWheelZoom passed into PanZoomLayer has a stable identity across renders that do not change zoom-gesture-relevant state",
          "PanZoomLayer.js’s wheel effect (lines 304-404) no longer tears down/reinstalls on every render during an active zoom gesture",
          "accumulatedDelta/isThrottling/throttleTimeout survive across the duration of one continuous wheel gesture"
        ],
