        "title": "Tracked-previous-level guard, or move the fold to a transform-based animation?",
        "body": "Task 1 needs one of two designs picked before implementation: (a) a per-instance previous-level ref that suppresses the transition unless the level actually changed this render, or (b) moving the discrete semantic fold onto an inner element's transform: scale() so continuous zoom (width/height, immediate) and discrete folding (transform, animated) stop sharing a CSS channel entirely. (a) is smaller and more surgical; (b) is architecturally cleaner but touches more of the render path, including PassiveGraphSemanticView's multiple branches.",
